## CROSS-MODEL SYNTHESIS

### Structural Patterns Across All 12 Models

**What separates survivors from the 81% who quit:**
1. **Distribution before product.** Every precedent (ranchwork.com, TypingMind, Nomad List, Lenny's Newsletter) had a DISTRIBUTION CHANNEL before building. SEO, audience, or community presence. Building first = gambling. [T]
2. **Toll booth > content.** Models 1, 3, 5, 10, 11 are TOLL BOOTHS — sit between parties who need each other. Structurally superior to content businesses because toll booths grow with transactions, not creator output. [T]
3. **Lindy > novelty.** Job boards, directories, calculators, data services existed 20+ years. Novel types (AI wrappers, crypto) have higher upside but <3yr Lindy. At $0-500 capital, you can't afford novelty bets. [T]

### Founder-Specific Ranking (phamt-260507)

**Primary strength:** Dev skills + Vietnam cost base
**Primary weakness:** No existing audience, $0-500 capital, English as L2, no US professional network

**RECOMMENDED PRIORITY ORDER:**
1. **Model 5 (Calculator tool)** — zero capital, pure code leverage, sleep-test pass, no audience needed (SEO acquires), AI-resistant distribution moat. BUILD THIS FIRST.
2. **Model 1 (Niche job board)** — if calculator validates, layer job board on same vertical. Network effect compounds.
3. **Model 11 (Monitoring service)** — pure code, sticky churn, parallel to above.

**DO NOT start with:** Models 4, 6, 8, 12 — require audience/network/English fluency/sales skill not yet in founder profile.

